I didn't understand very much of it, but what I did understand,

01:00:43.560 --> 01:00:44.940
I don't know, I panicked and called you.

01:00:45.020 --> 01:00:45.540
So here I am.

01:00:47.740 --> 01:00:48.360
What's your promise?

01:01:02.590 --> 01:01:03.900
Hot lagers for this kitchen.

01:01:04.570 --> 01:01:05.690
Yeah, well, two nice ones on ice.

01:01:05.790 --> 01:01:07.490
You know you haven't because I've just sold them.

01:01:08.130 --> 01:01:10.070
Hang on to those in case Mr. McGuire will do them.

01:01:10.380 --> 01:01:10.920
I heard you.

01:01:11.060 --> 01:01:11.880
You never hear anything.

01:01:12.260 --> 01:01:13.460
I'll keep ice in this weather.

01:01:13.760 --> 01:01:14.680
No, three hot scotches.

01:01:14.680 --> 01:01:15.980
Get some more ice now over me.

01:01:16.180 --> 01:01:17.240
A personal, not professional.

01:01:17.780 --> 01:01:18.480
Why, Mr. McGuire?

01:01:18.580 --> 01:01:19.020
That's right.

01:01:21.270 --> 01:01:21.890
I need you, Dad.

01:01:21.990 --> 01:01:22.870
You need that, so drink it.

01:01:23.160 --> 01:01:24.020
Put them on the slate, may we?

01:01:28.200 --> 01:01:29.860
Funny story on my way to the park this morning.

01:01:30.090 --> 01:01:30.470
How funny.

01:01:32.340 --> 01:01:33.540
What's the nutation of the Earth?

01:01:34.020 --> 01:01:34.380
Nutation?

01:01:34.540 --> 01:01:37.840
Well, it's a slight oscillation on the Earth's axis,

01:01:38.240 --> 01:01:40.240
caused by the pull of the sun and the moon on the equator.

01:01:40.240 --> 01:01:40.580
It's changed.

01:01:41.260 --> 01:01:42.680
You see, there's a slight bulge on the...

01:01:43.500 --> 01:01:45.680
There's also an item here about axis rotation.

01:01:45.860 --> 01:01:47.760
There's been an 11-degree variation, whatever that may mean.

01:01:48.000 --> 01:01:48.720
Where did this come from?

01:01:48.780 --> 01:01:49.700
Never mind where it came from.

01:01:49.840 --> 01:01:50.300
Translate it.

01:01:50.920 --> 01:01:51.640
It means I was right.

01:01:52.220 --> 01:01:52.580
Congratulations.

01:01:53.920 --> 01:01:55.260
They've shifted the tilt of the Earth.

01:01:56.660 --> 01:01:59.320
The stupid, crazy, irresponsible bastards.

01:02:01.690 --> 01:02:02.630
They've finally done it.

01:02:07.050 --> 01:02:07.870
Normal angle of tilt.

01:02:08.640 --> 01:02:11.780
An 11 degree variation would put it this way, or there.

01:02:11.940 --> 01:02:14.220
We don't know whether it's east or west.

01:02:14.490 --> 01:02:14.690
Nope.

01:02:15.320 --> 01:02:17.500
A weather line theory would indicate an east to west tilt.

01:02:18.240 --> 01:02:19.360
Where'd you get this story, Stenning?

01:02:19.460 --> 01:02:20.860
I prefer you not to ask, sir.

01:02:21.780 --> 01:02:24.300
Give me Sir John Kelly, either at his office or at his home.

01:02:24.600 --> 01:02:25.840
Whenever he is, I want to talk to him.

01:02:25.880 --> 01:02:26.900
Does this come from your new contact?

01:02:26.900 --> 01:02:27.960
Never mind where it comes from.

01:02:28.040 --> 01:02:28.860
You take my word.

01:02:28.980 --> 01:02:29.640
That's the story.

01:02:30.380 --> 01:02:33.220
What can this do to us, Bill, apart from altering the Earth's climates?

01:02:33.690 --> 01:02:35.550
Monkeying around with nature on this scale.

01:02:35.880 --> 01:02:37.240
Who knows what the implications are.

01:02:37.500 --> 01:02:38.440
Well, what do you think?

01:02:39.520 --> 01:02:40.100
Prefer not to.

01:02:41.740 --> 01:02:44.260
Yes, I didn't ask for the PRO.

01:02:45.560 --> 01:02:46.480
All right, put him through.

01:02:46.680 --> 01:02:46.960
Who is it?

01:02:47.100 --> 01:02:47.580
Holroyd, sir.

01:02:48.540 --> 01:02:49.940
Get Jaco in, get everybody in.

01:02:50.550 --> 01:02:53.700
Holroyd, this is Jefferson, the editor of the Daily Express here.

01:02:55.020 --> 01:02:58.160
Yes, well, you can tell Sir John that he has the choice of being disturbed now

01:02:58.160 --> 01:02:59.900
or when he reads his morning paper.

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:02.240
We're going to print whether he talks or not.

01:03:02.920 --> 01:03:03.800
Bill, get moving.

01:03:04.180 --> 01:03:06.740
I want a pictorial panorama of the world as it's going to be

01:03:06.740 --> 01:03:08.700
with the new climatic zones and all the rest of it change.

01:03:09.070 --> 01:03:10.330
Steny, come in on this phone.

01:03:10.630 --> 01:03:11.170
Take this down.

01:03:12.030 --> 01:03:13.590
Sir John Kelly, Jefferson here.

01:03:14.120 --> 01:03:15.880
I'd like a statement and I'd like it now.

01:03:17.300 --> 01:03:18.100
Nothing's impossible.

01:03:18.480 --> 01:03:21.200
Not even an 11-degree tilt in the globe's axis.

01:03:22.310 --> 01:03:24.550
Yes, that's precisely what we're going to print.

01:04:31.980 --> 01:04:38.220
Morning, sir. What about all this then? World tips over. Fog, cyclone and flood.

01:04:52.300 --> 01:04:54.170
What else? I don't want to hear. I don't want to know.

01:04:54.190 --> 01:04:56.950
It had to come out, Jeannie. You couldn't sit on a thing like this.

01:04:57.130 --> 01:04:57.830
That's right. That's right.

01:04:58.400 --> 01:04:59.880
But we didn't use your name, Jeannie.

01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:01.080
Nobody used your name.

01:05:01.240 --> 01:05:02.980
Who cares about my name? My name's nothing.

01:05:03.140 --> 01:05:04.140
It's my trust you've used.

01:05:05.020 --> 01:05:05.640
All right, I'm ready.

01:05:07.110 --> 01:05:07.590
Who are you?

01:05:08.000 --> 01:05:09.060
I'm a security officer.

01:05:09.260 --> 01:05:10.400
Now, wait a minute. Where are you taking her?

01:05:10.540 --> 01:05:12.200
For the moment, into preventative custody.

01:05:12.480 --> 01:05:12.720
For what?

01:05:12.940 --> 01:05:13.720
Can we go now, please?

01:05:14.560 --> 01:05:15.460
What the hell are you preventing?

01:05:15.640 --> 01:05:16.400
It's happened, man.

01:05:16.770 --> 01:05:18.990
You've got the head weathercock sitting on the biggest adult head

01:05:18.990 --> 01:05:20.050
the human race has ever laid.

01:05:20.150 --> 01:05:21.670
Leave it alone, please. It's not in your business.

01:05:21.970 --> 01:05:23.410
You've got these bloody bombs on

01:05:23.410 --> 01:05:25.430
as though they were falling scribbs on bonfire night.

01:05:25.530 --> 01:05:26.530
You want your people a secret?

01:05:27.400 --> 01:05:28.100
Fine, fine.

01:05:28.200 --> 01:05:29.780
So they stick the kid into preventative custody.

01:05:30.000 --> 01:05:32.160
Oh, cool off. I know it's hot, but cool off.

01:05:32.160 --> 01:05:35.440
Never mind the data on leukemia or infant mortality or strontium G

01:05:35.440 --> 01:05:37.460
or any of the other clinical facts of mass suicide.

01:05:37.600 --> 01:05:39.500
Just stick some kid in a cell and everything will be all right.

01:05:39.660 --> 01:05:41.020
You've gone right about it just like that.

01:05:41.140 --> 01:05:44.560
Oh, sure. Now they want to read about the filthy self-destructive force

01:05:44.560 --> 01:05:48.340
humanity carries around rotting in its belly now when it's too late.

01:05:48.500 --> 01:05:50.560
It's never too late for a good story well written.

01:05:50.560 --> 01:05:52.880
The human race has been poisoning itself for years

01:05:52.880 --> 01:05:55.100
with a great big smile on its fat face.

01:05:55.320 --> 01:05:56.360
Well, that's how it is, Pete.

01:05:56.560 --> 01:05:58.740
People don't care about the news until it becomes personal.

01:05:58.740 --> 01:05:59.980
Well, it has become personal for me.

01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:29.890
me? Isn't there anything you can do? What else is there to do? I've made my will. Look, Pete, they're just a bit hysterical like the rest of us. They let her out in a few days. Let her out to do what? Who's going to give her a job? No problem there. We'll give her a job. While it all still lasts, we might as well have full employment. I felt it necessary to speak to you all.

01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:33.710
if only to stop the many wild and irresponsible rumors

01:06:34.290 --> 01:06:36.330
precipitated by a general lack of fact.

01:06:37.740 --> 01:06:41.440
There has indeed been a displacement in the direction of the polar axis.

01:06:42.340 --> 01:06:45.080
But it is not a catastrophe, nor is it the millennium.

01:06:46.130 --> 01:06:48.490
Geologists and astronomers have long had evidence

01:06:48.490 --> 01:06:51.660
that the tilt of the Earth has been altered more than once

01:06:51.660 --> 01:06:55.230
in the history of its evolution, and it has survived them all.

01:06:56.340 --> 01:06:58.720
Now, what does this mean to us in our daily lives?

01:07:00.730 --> 01:07:04.680
Some of the seasons, as we know them, may be disturbed and change their intensity.

01:07:08.640 --> 01:07:12.000
Undoubtedly brought some regions nearer to the polar circle.

01:07:15.730 --> 01:07:18.110
Others have been carried further from it.

01:07:18.510 --> 01:07:25.000
With the utmost confidence, the world scientists can produce solutions

01:07:25.000 --> 01:07:28.240
for any of the climatic problems we are likely to meet.

01:07:30.030 --> 01:07:36.790
I know that many of you are blaming the combined effects of nuclear tests for this disturbance to the motion of the Earth.

01:07:36.910 --> 01:07:43.160
I must tell you that the majority of the world's scientists deny that this is the cause.

01:07:44.610 --> 01:07:51.580
However, I would be failing in my duty if I did not admit to you that there are many others who believe it could have been.

01:07:52.780 --> 01:07:59.880
But whatever the rights, whatever the wrongs, four major powers have now reached unconditional agreement.

01:08:00.730 --> 01:08:07.170
Cease or further test elements, manufacture and work on clear projects.

01:08:07.870 --> 01:08:09.050
What they'll do to get votes.

01:08:09.440 --> 01:08:12.920
I ask you now to face the future calmly and constructive,

01:08:14.000 --> 01:08:15.820
remembering that here in Britain, at least,

01:08:16.640 --> 01:08:18.710
the weather is something we are used to coping with.

01:08:19.460 --> 01:08:20.640
Wonder who writes his punchlines.

01:08:20.940 --> 01:08:23.080
The old boy only do all the laughs he can get if this heat keeps up.

01:08:23.520 --> 01:08:25.340
Now leave it on, mate. Let's see the forecast.

01:08:25.800 --> 01:08:27.080
Yes, it's always so right.

01:08:27.600 --> 01:08:29.640
I wouldn't mind the heat of this stupid old fool.

01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:30.860
I remember to order the ice.

01:08:30.940 --> 01:08:31.720
I did order it.

01:08:31.740 --> 01:08:32.380
Now, where is it?

01:08:32.930 --> 01:08:34.470
I don't deliver it, Mae.

01:08:35.060 --> 01:08:36.180
It's real bikini weather, Mae.

01:08:36.440 --> 01:08:36.600
Yeah.

01:08:36.780 --> 01:08:40.780
All this heat's making you not bear like furrowness.

01:08:41.040 --> 01:08:42.760
No point in holding a hot glass. Have another one.

01:08:43.410 --> 01:08:44.270
No, I'm going back to the office.

01:08:49.640 --> 01:08:50.380
What's on your mind?

01:08:51.170 --> 01:08:52.510
Do you think Geoff would give me an advance?

01:08:53.080 --> 01:08:53.760
Depends how much.

01:08:54.640 --> 01:08:56.240
However much it'd cost to get her a good lawyer.

01:08:56.320 --> 01:08:57.300
Ah, stop worrying.

01:08:57.460 --> 01:08:59.020
She'll only be in for a week, too, at most.

01:08:59.140 --> 01:08:59.980
They're just going through them.

01:09:00.120 --> 01:09:02.000
She didn't break the story, Bill, I did.

01:09:02.100 --> 01:09:03.680
If they're going to charge anyone, it should be me.

01:09:04.050 --> 01:09:06.030
So if you brought in the feet of the century...

01:09:06.030 --> 01:09:06.630
Captain Gardner.

01:09:07.700 --> 01:09:08.300
What is it, Dick?

01:09:08.480 --> 01:09:09.760
No, not as dry as a bone.

01:09:09.880 --> 01:09:10.760
They think it's all going up.

01:09:33.070 --> 01:09:33.350
Good night.

01:12:01.280 --> 01:12:02.360
This is the editorial floor.

01:12:02.970 --> 01:12:05.070
Bandon all hope ye who enter here.

01:12:05.230 --> 01:12:06.790
This where I work?

01:12:07.080 --> 01:12:08.680
Through the newsroom and down into the library.

01:12:09.140 --> 01:12:11.660
By the way, I'd better warn you about some of these newsroom

01:12:11.660 --> 01:12:12.040
characters.

01:12:12.300 --> 01:12:13.380
I'm a big girl now.

01:12:13.580 --> 01:12:14.180
That's what I mean.

01:12:14.240 --> 01:12:16.490
Mr. McGuire, if you ever want any extra water.

01:12:16.770 --> 01:12:17.350
Never drink it.

01:12:17.650 --> 01:12:18.750
I mean, I've got a contact.

01:12:18.950 --> 01:12:20.310
Five gallon drum only costs a pound.

01:12:20.410 --> 01:12:20.650
Great.

01:12:20.750 --> 01:12:22.190
We'll celebrate with two iced cokes.

01:12:22.350 --> 01:12:23.630
They're fetching four bob apiece now.

01:12:23.730 --> 01:12:24.110
Are they?

01:12:24.190 --> 01:12:25.310
I'll get them soon as I drop these.

01:12:25.450 --> 01:12:26.570
Well, tell them they're bloody robbers.

01:12:30.000 --> 01:12:31.760
He's out on a date, if that makes any difference.

01:12:32.510 --> 01:12:33.370
Not to me, it doesn't.

01:12:33.810 --> 01:12:35.510
Look, Jeannie, you can't go on blaming him

01:12:35.510 --> 01:12:36.830
for blowing that story you gave him.

01:12:37.140 --> 01:12:38.200
Can we change the subject?

01:12:38.440 --> 01:12:40.240
No journalist would have any right not to.

01:12:40.460 --> 01:12:40.880
I agree.

01:12:41.590 --> 01:12:42.990
Tell me, do I always come in this way,

01:12:43.070 --> 01:12:44.590
or is there some sort of tradesman's entrance?

01:12:44.850 --> 01:12:45.990
Yes, I'll mind my own business.

01:12:46.590 --> 01:12:49.690
Now, these are the legal gentlemen, the Brothers Prodenos.

01:12:51.130 --> 01:12:52.310
This is the Chief Buncheth.

01:12:52.550 --> 01:12:55.460
Jacko, Miss Craig, library and standby switchboard.

01:12:55.560 --> 01:12:56.140
Hello, and welcome.

01:12:56.360 --> 01:12:56.680
Thank you.

01:12:57.160 --> 01:12:58.880
All I can say is, whoever took your press pictures

01:12:58.880 --> 01:12:59.460
ought to be fried.

01:12:59.620 --> 01:12:59.980
What's the...

01:13:00.000 --> 01:13:02.300
Hospital emergency water trucks rammed.

01:13:02.340 --> 01:13:03.460
Yeah, they grabbed 5,000 gallons.

01:13:03.520 --> 01:13:05.520
Marvellous, isn't it? I can remember when it used to be money.

01:13:06.190 --> 01:13:07.850
I must say, this is all a bit frightening.

01:13:08.090 --> 01:13:09.850
Nothing to worry about unless you own a reservoir.

01:13:10.230 --> 01:13:11.030
No, I meant the job.

01:13:11.210 --> 01:13:14.140
Oh, you're getting up to it. The chief librarian's a nice guy.

01:13:14.300 --> 01:13:16.940
He'll put you right. If there's any special problem, there's always me.

01:13:17.640 --> 01:13:18.080
Poor Pete.

01:13:19.340 --> 01:13:21.900
Everything's filed here from the atom bomb to Zen Buddhism.

01:13:22.550 --> 01:13:25.270
Bill, I appreciate the motives, but don't try and restart anything.

01:13:25.410 --> 01:13:26.450
It's very, very over.

01:13:26.630 --> 01:13:28.850
A breakdown, Jeannie. What do you want him in the penitent's parade,

01:13:29.030 --> 01:13:29.970
walking barefooted down...

01:13:30.030 --> 01:13:34.820
fleet street i don't want him anywhere this is no time to waste time well he ain't wasting it he's

01:13:34.820 --> 01:13:42.850
ours on a date in battersea park with his kid oh miss craig you found your way eh mr mcguire brought

01:13:42.850 --> 01:13:48.450
me yes i shouldn't think we'd ever be lonely down here now look after her archie she's a bright

01:13:48.450 --> 01:13:56.960
girl just a sense of proportion that's a bit bent here we are eight shillings worth of deliciously

01:13:57.360 --> 01:13:58.520
Take that to Miss Craig, will you?

01:13:59.380 --> 01:13:59.900
What's the matter, kid?

01:14:00.570 --> 01:14:02.420
Hmm? Hey? I'm all right, sir.

01:14:03.350 --> 01:14:04.910
Holy smoke, look at these temperatures.

01:14:05.310 --> 01:14:08.230
Mexico Delta, 145.6 degrees Fahrenheit.

01:14:08.630 --> 01:14:10.790
USA, Texas, 141.3.

01:14:11.280 --> 01:14:12.700
Rome, 139.

01:14:12.820 --> 01:14:14.640
This famine death count's pretty terrifying.

01:14:14.640 --> 01:14:16.040
I just don't get this lack of water.

01:14:16.540 --> 01:14:18.360
What about all this extra polar ice that's melting?

01:14:18.500 --> 01:14:19.760
Well, the heat's taking it up as vapor.

01:14:20.020 --> 01:14:21.740
Yeah, but I think it ought to come down again sometimes.

01:14:22.040 --> 01:14:24.440
It has, and when it does, pray you're on high ground, huh?

01:14:33.070 --> 01:14:34.670
Dave, I just came from Battersea Park.

01:14:34.690 --> 01:14:35.950
Personally, I prefer Brighton.

01:14:36.570 --> 01:14:37.350
Look, something's going on.

01:14:37.470 --> 01:14:38.530
If you're not interested, to hell with it.

01:14:38.710 --> 01:14:39.770
Unwind, for God's sake.

01:14:39.850 --> 01:14:41.070
How do I know if I'm interested?

01:14:41.230 --> 01:14:41.890
What sort of something?

01:14:42.280 --> 01:14:44.740
Well, they're putting up long sheds, you know, the army type.

01:14:45.030 --> 01:14:47.390
And there's trucks full of piping and shower bath fittings.

01:14:47.780 --> 01:14:50.320
500-gallon water tanks, complete with purifying systems.

01:14:50.500 --> 01:14:50.800
Battersea Park.

01:14:50.940 --> 01:14:51.020
Yeah.

01:14:51.380 --> 01:14:54.560
And Hyde Park, Richmond, Wimbledon, Highgate, Hampstead, most of the open spaces.

01:14:54.680 --> 01:14:55.200
You've seen them?

01:14:55.320 --> 01:14:56.000
Only Battersea.

01:14:56.250 --> 01:14:57.550
But I talked to one of the drivers.

01:14:57.670 --> 01:14:59.910
In the last few days, he delivered similar gear to the others.

01:15:00.030 --> 01:15:00.470
For what?

01:15:00.780 --> 01:15:01.920
I don't know. I never got that far.

01:15:02.000 --> 01:15:03.500
The foreman came up shouting security.

01:15:03.620 --> 01:15:04.040
Any ideas?

01:15:04.710 --> 01:15:06.650
Yes. Community washing centers.

01:15:07.030 --> 01:15:07.490
Good God.

01:15:07.690 --> 01:15:08.590
Why, you got ugly neighbors?

01:15:09.360 --> 01:15:11.840
