like they're about to cut all running water yeah but I'd like him to talk to

01:15:51.020 --> 01:15:55.070
you before he writes anything listen you're putting up community showers in

01:15:55.070 --> 01:15:59.960
all the parks all right I'll send them in Pete go tell the old man

01:16:01.600 --> 01:16:02.560
Well, we're getting pictures.

01:16:02.800 --> 01:16:03.740
What about the hospital?

01:16:04.320 --> 01:16:04.880
Well, try them.

01:16:05.160 --> 01:16:07.140
If it's going to happen, they're bound to know about it.

01:16:07.200 --> 01:16:08.360
They'll have made special arrangements.

01:16:09.210 --> 01:16:11.390
And if anything comes through on the tapes, let me know.

01:16:11.960 --> 01:16:13.080
You actually saw these showers?

01:16:13.200 --> 01:16:14.460
About 50 of them in the Balassie Hut.

01:16:14.620 --> 01:16:16.720
I wouldn't like you to make guesses about things like this.

01:16:16.860 --> 01:16:18.020
There's too much panic about as it is.

01:16:18.040 --> 01:16:19.780
Sorry, Clive McCready on the phone from Moscow.

01:16:20.000 --> 01:16:20.320
Moscow?

01:16:20.540 --> 01:16:20.980
It's urgent.

01:16:21.100 --> 01:16:21.780
Very bad line.

01:16:21.920 --> 01:16:23.400
Oh, I wonder if it got through at all.

01:16:24.150 --> 01:16:24.470
Clive?

01:16:24.900 --> 01:16:25.200
Hello?

01:16:26.190 --> 01:16:26.510
Clive?

01:16:27.570 --> 01:16:29.050
Yes, I can't hear you.

01:16:30.860 --> 01:16:40.610
yes uh-huh yes i've got it i only wish i didn't believe it i expect you'd like to

01:16:40.610 --> 01:16:46.660
come home now is anything still flying well it's up to you you can if you wish

01:17:00.830 --> 01:17:03.060
Jacko! Conference!

01:17:03.780 --> 01:17:04.900
Jacko, where the hell are you?

01:17:05.340 --> 01:17:05.680
Yes, sir?

01:17:05.950 --> 01:17:07.190
In here. Get a move on.

01:17:08.520 --> 01:17:10.570
Miss Evans, get the old man.

01:17:10.670 --> 01:17:12.650
I think he's at Cherkley, but wherever he is, I'll find him.

01:17:12.810 --> 01:17:13.110
Yes, sir.

01:17:13.190 --> 01:17:13.750
You want me to wait?

01:17:13.910 --> 01:17:25.230
You have a family, don't you?

01:17:25.350 --> 01:17:27.500
A son.

01:17:29.860 --> 01:17:29.960
I do.

01:17:30.000 --> 01:17:31.160
Get them to the country if you can.

01:17:31.320 --> 01:17:33.420
I don't think things in the cities are going to be too pleasant.

01:17:33.560 --> 01:17:35.420
I brought the dummy in case you want to turn that up.

01:17:35.560 --> 01:17:36.360
On the direct line.

01:17:38.940 --> 01:17:39.520
Good evening, sir.

01:17:40.590 --> 01:17:42.470
Well, the Russians have just about topped everything.

01:17:43.460 --> 01:17:44.860
MacReady got through from Moscow.

01:17:45.430 --> 01:17:47.290
They held an international press conference,

01:17:47.430 --> 01:17:48.830
had their top scientists present.

01:17:50.010 --> 01:17:52.730
They say that those two bangs did more than alter the tilt.

01:17:53.130 --> 01:17:55.270
They made an 11-degree shift in our orbit.

01:17:57.850 --> 01:17:59.730
And we're moving towards the sun.

01:18:02.140 --> 01:18:04.580
Well, I can't see what they've gained by making it up.

01:18:05.420 --> 01:18:07.840
They say Western scientists have known about this all along,

01:18:07.940 --> 01:18:10.020
but we're trying to work something out before they broke it.

01:18:10.480 --> 01:18:14.260
It's not through on the agencies yet, but it's bound to be any moment.

01:18:15.140 --> 01:18:16.180
No, of course not.

01:18:17.350 --> 01:18:19.270
No, that's the way I was going to play it.

01:18:20.340 --> 01:18:22.160
I'll have it put through to you.

01:18:26.960 --> 01:18:28.820
Anyone want a recap, or did you get it?

01:18:28.900 --> 01:18:29.960
We got it, but what the hell?

01:18:30.190 --> 01:18:35.180
we do with it start with it's two lines of 120 point across eight columns I'm not

01:18:35.180 --> 01:18:38.320
up on my sci-fi so we're orbiting towards the Sun but how many billion

01:18:38.320 --> 01:18:47.550
light years that's true I'd say there's about four months for what before there's

01:18:47.550 --> 01:18:52.110
a delightful smell in the universe of charcoal mankind you really mean four

01:18:52.110 --> 01:18:57.540
months according to the temperature rises in the last few weeks yes that's the

01:18:57.540 --> 01:18:59.640
message about another 300 deadline

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:01.260
Is that what we say in tomorrow's paper?

01:19:01.360 --> 01:19:03.200
Tomorrow we report the news, the facts.

01:19:03.620 --> 01:19:05.240
We leave prophecy to the street corner cranks.

01:19:05.540 --> 01:19:07.790
Bill, you and Sandy, start arranging interviews

01:19:07.790 --> 01:19:09.530
with top scientists, Cockcroft, Penny.

01:19:09.810 --> 01:19:11.490
If you can get a call through to Calcutta,

01:19:11.630 --> 01:19:12.730
Haldane might break silence.

01:19:13.050 --> 01:19:15.300
Pete, you'll get busy on the no water angle.

01:19:15.700 --> 01:19:17.680
Everything affected, sanitation, electricity,

01:19:17.960 --> 01:19:20.260
power plants, even down to car radiators.

01:19:21.030 --> 01:19:23.390
And keep the tone of the paper reasonably optimistic,

01:19:23.550 --> 01:19:23.890
understand?

01:19:24.290 --> 01:19:25.330
It's going to be all right.

01:19:25.660 --> 01:19:25.980
That's it.

01:19:26.950 --> 01:19:28.190
Sir, there's an agency flash.

01:19:28.290 --> 01:19:29.270
Yes, we just had it.

01:19:29.310 --> 01:19:29.970
In every possible...

01:19:36.060 --> 01:19:36.740
Home, please.

01:19:39.820 --> 01:19:42.120
I was going on holiday next month. Do you think I should cancel it?

01:19:42.160 --> 01:19:43.500
The only thing that cancels is your life insurance.

01:19:43.640 --> 01:19:44.440
Set up and have an orgy.

01:19:44.560 --> 01:19:46.520
Nice public-spirited advice will do me a favor.

01:19:46.520 --> 01:19:47.960
Can't let anything be done, Mr. McGrath?

01:19:48.040 --> 01:19:49.500
Yes, there's something you can do right away.

01:19:49.660 --> 01:19:50.500
Pop off to the library.

01:19:50.620 --> 01:19:52.220
Bring me everything they've got on melting points.

01:19:52.480 --> 01:19:53.000
Melting points?

01:19:53.400 --> 01:19:57.340
Yes, and the temperatures that put everything from steel to my glass eye starts to melt.

01:19:58.550 --> 01:19:59.650
I suppose it couldn't be a mistake.

01:20:01.340 --> 01:20:03.740
It is. The daddy of all mistakes.

01:20:05.100 --> 01:20:07.480
Funny how when the chopper falls, everyone just accepts it.

01:20:08.200 --> 01:20:09.700
What else when it's your neck under it?

01:20:10.130 --> 01:20:13.350
The fellow here from Leeds says he's found a method of extracting water from the atmosphere.

01:20:14.390 --> 01:20:15.650
Oh, as you were, he's been certified.

01:20:17.700 --> 01:20:20.280
Jeff said to get the kid out of town, it might be a bit easier in the country.

01:20:20.480 --> 01:20:21.120
Yes, it might.

01:20:21.560 --> 01:20:23.160
Couldn't get my old woman away from the garden.

01:20:23.280 --> 01:20:24.660
She's got about six pennies of sweet peas.

01:20:24.760 --> 01:20:26.540
She'll be out buying black market water for them.

01:20:27.290 --> 01:20:28.170
Which reminds me.

01:20:28.870 --> 01:20:29.670
It's highly illegal, too.

01:20:30.120 --> 01:20:30.780
No, thanks.

01:20:31.620 --> 01:20:32.080
Quite right.

01:20:32.280 --> 01:20:33.720
I suppose they'll do something, won't they, Bill?

01:20:34.800 --> 01:20:34.940
What?

01:20:35.490 --> 01:20:36.730
Well, something. They've got to do something.

01:20:36.830 --> 01:20:37.890
They can't just let...

01:20:38.140 --> 01:20:40.310
A piece to write, haven't you?

01:20:40.350 --> 01:20:41.250
I know what I'd like to write.

01:20:41.410 --> 01:20:42.650
You can't. This is a family newspaper.

01:20:42.770 --> 01:20:44.810
We're all so bloody clever at outsmarting nature.

01:20:44.930 --> 01:20:46.490
Anything you can split, I can split better.

01:20:46.860 --> 01:20:47.880
Do you know what I'd do if I were you?

01:20:48.040 --> 01:20:48.160
What?

01:20:48.660 --> 01:20:50.440
Some special data waiting for you in the library.

01:20:50.580 --> 01:20:55.250
An hour ago, I brought her.

01:20:56.850 --> 01:20:58.230
Well, in that case, we'll just skip the library.

01:20:58.410 --> 01:20:59.970
You know she hasn't spoken...

01:21:00.000 --> 01:21:01.760
Well, how the hell can she speak to you in separate rooms?

01:21:04.240 --> 01:21:08.420
Well, I need some data anyway.

01:21:10.350 --> 01:21:14.680
We'll need whatever we can get.

01:21:15.940 --> 01:21:17.100
You see, they're all cross-filed.

01:21:17.460 --> 01:21:20.500
You have to remember what names are connected with what subjects and vice versa.

01:21:21.020 --> 01:21:27.230
Any time you want any help. I'm just getting Mr. Maguire's stuff, sir.

01:21:31.240 --> 01:21:32.370
Well, thanks.

01:21:36.540 --> 01:21:36.800
Yes?

01:21:37.150 --> 01:21:38.030
I need some...

01:21:38.090 --> 01:21:38.510
Pete.

01:21:40.420 --> 01:21:40.760
I need you, Jean.

01:21:42.570 --> 01:21:43.130
I need you, too.

01:22:21.020 --> 01:22:25.020
We are now supported by the Prime Minister at 9 o'clock tonight.

01:22:30.760 --> 01:22:31.100
Bye-bye.

01:23:01.820 --> 01:23:04.220
I'm sorry, sir, no entry. You'd better close this jump.

01:23:04.400 --> 01:23:06.880
I'm meeting someone inside. Not during rationals.

01:23:07.250 --> 01:23:09.330
Yeah, but anyone inside will have to come out this way.

01:23:09.590 --> 01:23:11.730
Look, don't start having a go. It's no use arguing.

01:23:12.010 --> 01:23:13.510
You can't take those in. Leave them here.

01:23:13.900 --> 01:23:15.220
I want to save half my shower.

01:23:15.340 --> 01:23:17.280
You can't take water from here. This is a washing centre.

01:23:17.420 --> 01:23:21.020
I don't think it's all. I mean, like, we're all entitled to so much water, aren't we?

01:23:21.040 --> 01:23:22.520
Here's a washing. Leave them here.

01:23:22.700 --> 01:23:24.340
So who says if it goes over us or in us?

01:23:24.420 --> 01:23:25.160
Move on.

01:23:25.460 --> 01:23:26.320
No, no, no, no.

01:23:35.130 --> 01:23:39.000
Attention, please. There will be an emergency about...

01:23:54.940 --> 01:23:58.180
We're driving away now into the country.

01:23:58.440 --> 01:23:58.880
I know, Mike.

01:23:59.340 --> 01:23:59.960
I wanted to...

01:24:00.060 --> 01:24:01.600
To say goodbye to the ghost train.

01:24:01.720 --> 01:24:02.600
Well, there isn't time now.

01:24:02.700 --> 01:24:03.640
In any way, it's closed off.

01:24:04.060 --> 01:24:05.520
Will it be open again sometime?

01:24:05.960 --> 01:24:06.880
Yeah, maybe sometime.

01:24:08.270 --> 01:24:08.810
Mummy's here.

01:24:08.970 --> 01:24:10.070
Come and see Mummy.

01:24:11.580 --> 01:24:12.640
You can come with us.

01:24:13.100 --> 01:24:14.180
You come with us, Daddy.

01:24:14.620 --> 01:24:16.000
Make Daddy come with us, Mummy.

01:24:20.380 --> 01:24:21.320
Hello, Angie.

01:24:21.920 --> 01:24:23.300
Why can't Daddy come with us?

01:24:25.280 --> 01:24:27.440
Somebody's got to stay in reported when the ghost train starts again.

01:24:27.640 --> 01:24:28.540
We'd want to know that, wouldn't we?

01:24:28.980 --> 01:24:29.900
I suppose so.

01:24:31.630 --> 01:24:32.190
Staying in London.

01:24:32.910 --> 01:24:33.790
Paper goes on forever.

01:24:34.920 --> 01:24:36.080
When will I see you again?

01:24:39.060 --> 01:24:39.520
Quite soon.

01:24:40.230 --> 01:24:40.930
Come out and visit you.

01:24:41.030 --> 01:24:41.670
Now go on, off you go.

01:24:41.810 --> 01:24:43.180
I want to sit in front!

01:24:43.400 --> 01:24:44.900
All right, but don't wriggle the whole time.

01:24:47.280 --> 01:24:48.200
We ought to leave now, Angelo.

01:24:50.790 --> 01:24:51.010
Bye.

01:24:52.190 --> 01:24:57.760
You got water in those cans?

01:24:57.940 --> 01:24:58.810
We saved a little.

01:24:59.240 --> 01:24:59.940
Keep to the main road.

01:25:00.030 --> 01:25:01.010
The water gangs are pretty busy.

01:25:01.130 --> 01:25:01.930
I won't take chances.

01:25:03.250 --> 01:25:03.950
Well, good luck, Peter.

01:25:05.860 --> 01:25:07.180
It all seems pretty ridiculous now, doesn't it?

01:25:09.240 --> 01:25:10.060
Yeah, pretty ridiculous.

01:25:10.500 --> 01:25:11.160
Look after the kid.

01:25:12.530 --> 01:25:12.950
See you.

01:25:15.420 --> 01:25:15.620
Maybe.

01:26:11.230 --> 01:26:14.390
Try and get it clearer. Nothing much I can do, sir. We're using every known cut-out.

01:26:14.660 --> 01:26:16.700
You bet they'll have another power failure in the middle of it.

01:26:16.800 --> 01:26:18.260
It's all right, sir. We're running on our own generation.

01:26:18.480 --> 01:26:19.840
We'll have to wait for agency copy.

01:26:19.960 --> 01:26:21.440
Ronnie, hop over to PA and wait for it.

01:26:23.500 --> 01:26:23.860
Go on.

01:26:35.160 --> 01:26:36.340
Keep it quiet, please.

01:26:52.450 --> 01:26:55.740
Well, with his tongue, it's all swollen.

01:26:56.260 --> 01:26:57.260
All right, try and get a doctor.

01:28:04.090 --> 01:28:05.210
You just missed the good news.

01:28:05.350 --> 01:28:06.150
I heard it at the PA.

01:28:06.390 --> 01:28:07.730
Here's the full speech, official release.

01:28:07.930 --> 01:28:08.810
When's the big bang?

01:28:08.950 --> 01:28:09.950
Wednesday, 11 a.m.

01:28:10.200 --> 01:28:11.660
They've got to have their tea break first, you know.

01:28:12.070 --> 01:28:13.050
I don't think that's humorous.

01:28:13.150 --> 01:28:13.330
Don't you?

01:28:13.430 --> 01:28:14.230
Well, try this for a laugh.

01:28:14.370 --> 01:28:16.070
There's five cases of typhus in North London,

01:28:16.110 --> 01:28:17.030
and they're expecting more.

01:28:17.290 --> 01:28:17.610
Typhus?

01:28:17.860 --> 01:28:19.220
Yes, from black market water, mostly.

01:28:19.420 --> 01:28:20.220
Four pounds a gallon.

01:28:20.320 --> 01:28:21.300
Typhus, no extra charge.

01:28:21.850 --> 01:28:22.350
What happened, kid?

01:28:22.650 --> 01:28:23.470
Don't touch them, any of you.

01:28:23.550 --> 01:28:23.870
Keep away.

01:28:25.030 --> 01:28:25.570
Where's he live?

01:28:25.710 --> 01:28:26.250
Live, I don't know.

01:28:26.310 --> 01:28:26.890
North London, sir.

01:28:27.730 --> 01:28:28.210
What I thought.

01:28:28.850 --> 01:28:29.350
Call emergency.

01:28:29.710 --> 01:28:29.970
Get an...

01:28:30.000 --> 01:28:30.880
I'll get it.

01:28:31.540 --> 01:28:32.640
Poor little bastard.

01:28:33.320 --> 01:28:34.220
Well, this is all we needed.

01:28:34.870 --> 01:28:37.210
You'll have to see your staff's inoculated before anyone leaves.

01:28:37.470 --> 01:28:37.590
Of course.

01:28:37.830 --> 01:28:40.170
Well, at least we have a choice now, typhus or leukemia.

01:28:40.460 --> 01:28:41.360
What do you think, Bill?

01:28:41.770 --> 01:28:42.650
The bonds, I mean.

01:28:42.810 --> 01:28:43.870
You heard what the PM said?

01:28:43.970 --> 01:28:44.310
No one.

01:28:44.410 --> 01:28:46.430
Not even Bill Maguire can answer that one.

01:28:46.770 --> 01:28:47.710
And if it doesn't work?

01:28:48.150 --> 01:28:49.230
Evacuation by spaceship.

01:28:49.470 --> 01:28:50.430
All aboard for the moon.

01:28:50.590 --> 01:28:51.690
You want the best dead planets?

01:28:51.790 --> 01:28:52.190
We are them.

01:28:52.390 --> 01:28:52.890
What a slug.

01:28:53.690 --> 01:28:54.010
Peace.

01:28:54.250 --> 01:28:57.300
If that's your last will and testament, don't forget to leave me my car.

01:28:57.540 --> 01:28:59.500
I'm de-gutting the polluted water peddlers.

01:28:59.620 --> 01:28:59.960
Give us my...

01:29:01.020 --> 01:29:04.440
Plus the twelve pounds I paid for my water circulator I haven't even seen.

01:29:05.090 --> 01:29:06.350
You want some? I'm off it.

01:29:06.800 --> 01:29:09.790
So I've noticed. It's a beautiful thing to watch a woman reform a man.

01:29:09.930 --> 01:29:11.350
Only needed the earth to catch fire.

01:29:11.470 --> 01:29:12.150
Glad you approve.

01:29:12.490 --> 01:29:14.670
Well, if you've exhausted your repertoire of amusing quips,

01:29:14.730 --> 01:29:16.430
I'll go and collect the other half of the reform movement.

01:29:16.720 --> 01:29:18.040
Gone. Gone?

01:29:18.650 --> 01:29:20.450
Yeah, she collected enough water for a bath,

01:29:20.530 --> 01:29:22.430
and she was going to have it before you turned it into coffee.

01:29:22.970 --> 01:29:23.610
Can I use the car?

01:29:24.000 --> 01:29:25.480
Surely. I've forgotten how to drive it.

01:29:34.250 --> 01:29:37.190
Well, Jacko, read all about it, including the carbons, slash what you want.

01:29:37.310 --> 01:29:37.790
I'm going home.

01:29:37.890 --> 01:29:38.070
Home?

01:29:38.820 --> 01:29:40.240
Yes, I've done enough work for one lifetime.

01:29:40.320 --> 01:29:41.060
But you have to be injected.

01:29:41.220 --> 01:29:41.680
Against what?

01:29:41.840 --> 01:29:42.480
The end of the world?

01:29:53.740 --> 01:29:55.480
Keep moving, please, down to the embankment.

01:29:55.560 --> 01:29:56.180
The road's closed.

01:29:56.320 --> 01:29:57.380
Can I get back on to the other end?

01:29:57.500 --> 01:29:57.920
Not tonight.

01:29:58.020 --> 01:29:59.060
This district's out of bounds.

01:29:59.640 --> 01:29:59.980
For me to...

01:30:00.090 --> 01:30:02.450
No, there's some teenage kids kicking it up a bit.

01:30:02.680 --> 01:30:04.580
They lit a few fires, looted a bit of water.

01:30:05.160 --> 01:30:07.080
Where are you going, sir? Embankment Terrace.

01:30:07.610 --> 01:30:08.870
Okay, let this one through. Thanks.

01:30:09.230 --> 01:30:11.890
If you see any of them, keep driving. They're either drunk or drunk.

01:30:12.010 --> 01:30:15.090
Great party. And stay clear of Chelsea. They say it's pretty rough down there.

01:30:15.150 --> 01:30:16.250
It always was, wasn't it?

01:31:15.930 --> 01:31:16.890
What do you think you're doing?

01:31:17.350 --> 01:31:20.490
Making a great clean end, man! Real cool, clean finish!

01:31:46.240 --> 01:31:48.550
That's what you've been saving up for you, darling.

01:31:48.770 --> 01:31:49.190
Give me that.

01:31:51.070 --> 01:31:51.730
That's enough.

01:31:51.950 --> 01:31:52.350
Now, get on.

01:31:54.760 --> 01:31:59.800
I'm going to fall off and bath together.

01:32:31.850 --> 01:32:33.200
No, it's nothing. You?

01:32:33.560 --> 01:32:45.170
It was time I hit something. Go and barricade that door.

01:32:49.730 --> 01:32:50.810
They've all gone insane.

01:32:50.930 --> 01:32:55.960
Yeah, it's the new fashion. Did you hear the speech?

01:32:58.090 --> 01:32:58.650
I heard.

01:33:00.000 --> 01:33:01.340
Why did it all have to happen, Pete?

01:33:06.320 --> 01:33:10.010
It just had to, that's all. We're all too smart.

01:33:10.930 --> 01:33:12.390
All people want to do is live.

01:33:12.610 --> 01:33:13.370
I don't think so.

01:33:14.690 --> 01:33:15.690
I could understand why.

01:33:16.070 --> 01:33:17.890
A lot of people don't want to live. It's too difficult.

01:33:19.060 --> 01:33:19.940
Tired, they're frightened.

01:33:20.730 --> 01:33:23.490
I'd rather it was all over than go on worrying, being frightened,

01:33:24.480 --> 01:33:26.000
losing a bit more hope every day.

01:33:27.060 --> 01:33:29.680
But I don't.

01:33:30.760 --> 01:33:31.720
I don't want it to.

01:33:32.560 --> 01:33:33.420
Neither do I.

01:33:35.170 --> 01:33:35.450
Now.

01:34:00.830 --> 01:34:10.800
We are advised to stay in 47-1, minutes before countdown.

01:34:11.220 --> 01:34:27.660
We stood on the burning deck whence all but he had fled.

01:34:27.740 --> 01:34:29.970
My children, they fled to the machine room where the boot...

01:34:30.800 --> 01:34:31.640
But not the deck boy?

01:34:32.120 --> 01:34:33.960
He has an assignment. See you.

